=== 4.1 Special Abilities
==== Shared Opening: Unaware or Impeded
For Opportunist and Deadly Precision, choose an individual opponent against whom your declared approach materially benefits from an opening. They qualify if unaware of your presence, or if they are the participant whose action will receive pending Impede in the current volley (Core Rules §10.6).

Concealing hostile intent or the particular tactic does not by itself make you unnoticed. An opponent fighting your visible allies may still be unaware of you. An ongoing harmful status does not substitute for Impede, and an unrelated participant cannot supply eligibility. These abilities grant no inspection of the opposing script.

Check once after revealing actions and assigned actors and describing approaches, before either action rolls or resolves. A trumped opposing action does not qualify through Impede; unawareness may still qualify. For independent actions, eligibility established at this check lasts through the volley's resolution even when Impede expires during the opposing roll. Neither ability consumes or extends Impede. Meeting both triggers qualifies only once.

Outside scripted conflicts, check unawareness immediately before the roll or automatic resolution; Impede qualifies only where its conflict procedure exists. Resolve whether your action reveals your presence from what actually happens. Exposure may reveal you, but an indirect or concealed action need not do so without a fictional reason.

