==== Shared Limits and Stacking
Opportunist and Deadly Precision may benefit the same action. Opportunist's +1 Power may pay the discounted status price. Distinct flat offensive bonuses stack when each meets its requirements, each on its permitted component. Alternative status prices do not combine; calculate separately and use the lowest applicable price. Deadly Precision grants no general discount to other spending.

For an area effect, identify qualifying individual opponents. Opportunist grants at most +1 Power for the action. Deadly Precision grants at most +1 shared-Disposition loss or discounts one status purchase against one qualifying target. A shared area-status purchase uses normal pricing; the single-target discount cannot lower the whole area's price. Apply the area procedure's own Disposition adjustment separately (Core Rules §10.17).

These benefits can apply in any conflict type when the opening materially assists the fitting approach, including a precision-based Attack in an Argument. They advance only the declared objective and do not automatically inflict harmful statuses.

Neither ability grants an additional action, permits a trumped action to resolve, unlocks a harmful-status purchase, expands declared stakes or overrides independently resolving actions. Neither improves staking, killing strikes or another creature-specific finishing procedure unless that procedure expressly permits it. An unaware helpless or defeated target does not authorise an otherwise unavailable Attack or bypass a required finishing procedure.

